{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"8c13953c","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.006844,"end_time":"2026-11-18T20:05:18.483496","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-18T20:05:18.476652","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# Paper 1 revision experiments\n","\n","This notebook runs only the extra experiments for the revision of Paper 1. It does not repeat the main benchmark. The data split, partitions, model, local training and aggregators are copied from the main notebook (`fl_v3_q1_10client_lrtuned_sec23.ipynb`), so seeds 0-19 give the same partitions and initial models as before.\n","\n","- **R1.** Dataset audit with gradient boosting, XGBoost, random forest and k-NN.\n","- **R2.** The median used so far (`torch.median`, which returns the lower of the two middle values for 10 clients) next to the usual median (mean of the two middle values), on the clean sweep and the IID unreliable-client scenarios. Equal-weight mean at alpha=0.1.\n","- **R3.** Per-rule learning rates at alpha=0.1 with five tuning seeds and a wider grid, then the alpha=0.1 test runs.\n","- **R4.** CAFAD when poisoned clients report perfect accuracy (IID).\n","- **R5.** Label flipping at alpha=0.1 with the flipped clients chosen so that they hold 20% and 40% of the training records.\n","- **R6.** Record-level DP-SGD with the usual median.\n","- **R7.** The eta=0.01 runs repeated with the final preprocessing.\n","\n","Attach the V3 dataset and run all cells (about 4-5 hours; most of it is the DP part in R6). Each experiment saves a progress file after every run. If the session stops, add this notebook's output as an input and run all cells again; finished runs are skipped. To check the setup quickly, set `RUN_MODE = \"PILOT\"` first."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"36927c9c","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T20:05:18.496752Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T20:05:18.496306Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T20:05:19.655373Z","shell.execute_re